{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 1468 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D7"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the promethazine hydrochloride shortage on 2023-11-21 and it has remained on the list for 35 months as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D11", "E28"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our Corvale General inventory includes product from Zydus Lifesciences Limited (NDC 65841004110) and PD-Rx Pharmaceuticals, Inc. (NDC 43063040505).",
      "cites": ["E2", "E3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Zydus Lifesciences Limited plant (FEI 3002984011) on that label received an OAI classification letter dated 2019-11-14, which was 1468 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D7", "E20", "E25"]
    },
    {
      "text": "That same plant also received an earlier OAI classification letter dated 2016-06-09, 2721 days before the posting.",
      "cites": ["D6", "E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The PD-Rx Pharmaceuticals, Inc. plant (FEI 1641825) on our other label has only VAI inspections, most recently ending 2026-08-20.",
      "cites": ["E5", "E6", "E7", "E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The highest-ranked action by rule is to transfer 9 units from Corvale General to Corvale Lakeside, which would give Corvale Lakeside 14 days on hand while Corvale General retains two weeks of supply.",
      "cites": ["D8"]
    }
  ]
}
